{"availability":"available","full":"Kipper-Lang/Kipper","name":"Kipper","description":"The strongly typed programming languages implementing advanced runtime types & casts for a smoother development experience on the web!🦊✨ Made at HTL Leonding & JKU Linz ~ Open Dev Releases","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":29,"forks":5,"created":"2021-09-28T11:51:43Z","updated":"2026-10-05T18:14:07Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kipper-lang.org","topics":["antlr4","cli","compiler","javascript","kipper","language","nodejs","oop","programming-lang","programming-language","strict-typing","transpiler","typescript"],"demo":"https://play.kipper-lang.org/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:54.399Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:54.399Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:54.399Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T21:04:54.399Z","stars":29,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Kipper is a strongly typed language with Python flavour that targets both JavaScript & TypeScript. It aims to make web development straightforward, secure, and type-safe by combining stricter type handling, reflective runtime types, compiler checks, secure runtime casts, among many other features, for an all-round smooth development process on the web!","It compiles to a dependency-free output, bundling everything it needs into one neat package. It can be set up directly in your terminal using the Kipper CLI, with Node.js or run right in your browser. 🦊💻","For more details, you can read more about this project in the sections \"Goals & Planned Features\" and \"Why Kipper?\"."],"features":["Runtime Type Casting","Consistent Typing and Compile Time Cast Checks","Custom Runtime Types"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Kipper-Lang/Kipper/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9202e3411c7a12796d53b864606f1bd27228ecd6ce17bb72b88cc816165baf13","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:54.725Z"},"over